 "researcher_notes": "Not an existing row. The only roster row for this owner is the whole Colorado Interstate Gas system. The project is FERC docket CP01-1, in service October 2001. EIA lists it as CIG Front Range Expansion, 53.2 miles, 24 inch, 87 MMcf/d incremental, cost 58 million dollars (Aug 2026 release, Historical Projects sheet, Excel row 197). A separate FERC environmental notice from November 2000 independently states about 53.2 miles of 24 inch pipeline plus 2,825 hp of compression, with Fort Morgan storage work, in Weld, Adams and Morgan counties Colorado and Morton County Kansas. A 2001 CIG rate filing names CP01-1 as the Valley Line I Expansion. This is a different project from Valley Line CP01-45 (119 miles) and the 1998 Front Range line CP98-49. The pipe length may include storage gathering lines, so a person should check the split. The end point is not stated in the sources found, so EndLocation is left blank. Owner name is as the source spells it, with no gazetteer match. Route not found. Meets the length rule (53.2 miles is over 15.5). Operating line captured late rather than a new proposal."
